---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/digital-products';
const title = "Shopify cart recovery for digital product shops";
const desc = "Recover the sale without confusing purchase reminders with access delivery.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/for">← All store types</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify cart recovery for digital product shops</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Recover the sale without confusing purchase reminders with access delivery.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Separate checkout from access support</h2>
<p>An unpaid download checkout needs a clear description of what the buyer receives: file format, license scope, compatibility and how access arrives. A paid customer reporting a missing download needs fulfillment support instead. Keep delivery and onboarding messages outside the abandonment sequence; a payment must stop sales reminders even if access provisioning is delayed.</p>
<h2>Choose around entitlement data</h2>
<p>For a downloadable template, require the recovery tool to retain the selected license and bundle rather than show an unrelated catalog bestseller. For courses or memberships, document which system owns enrollment and renewals. Sequenzy or another lifecycle platform is a candidate only after a proposed integration check proves it receives the purchase and entitlement events you need; this guide does not establish that capability.</p>
<h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
<p>Create a paid-product checkout, a free resource checkout and a mixed physical/digital basket. Check eligibility separately, then complete a purchase while its reminder is queued. Inspect the destination and selected license on the recovery link. Ask support to trace a paid-but-no-access case; it should create an access investigation rather than another coupon.</p>
<h2>Offer economics and follow-through</h2>
<p>A digital product may still carry licensing, payment, affiliate and support costs. Calculate those before offering a discount; zero shipping does not mean zero marginal cost. After purchase, replace recovery with product-specific setup instructions and only introduce a cross-sell when it helps the buyer use the original purchase. Measure paid orders separately from free-resource acquisition.</p>
<h2>Check the trigger before replacing the tool</h2>
<p>Shopify distinguishes checkout recovery from earlier cart activity. Review <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/abandoned-checkouts">Shopify’s recovery eligibility</a> and inspect the actual workflow before comparing replacements. Proposed exercises above have not been performed.</p>
<p>Related decisions: <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">fashion stores</a> · <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">food and beverage brands</a>.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
